# {{ project.name }}

A web app built from small Rust microservices ([axum](https://github.com/tokio-rs/axum), SQLite) behind an edge reverse proxy, and a modular [Vue 3](https://vuejs.org) single-page app.

## Requirements

- Rust 1.89 or newer (`rustup`, https://rustup.rs)
- Node.js 24 or newer, npm 10 or newer
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}
- Docker 24 or newer with Docker Compose (only for running in a container)
{%- endif %}

## Quick start

```sh
npm install
npm run setup     # creates .env with a fresh MASTER_KEY (keeps an existing .env)
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}.{% if features.auth %} Register the first account: it becomes the administrator.{% endif %} The Vite dev server proxies `/api` to the edge on http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}, which routes each request to the service that owns its URL prefix (`services.json`).

Production-style run on a single port:

```sh
npm run build
npm start         # edge: API + built web app on http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}
```
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}

In Docker (one container runs every service and serves the web app):

```sh
docker compose up --build   # http://localhost:{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}
```
{%- endif %}

## Scripts

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Builds the Rust workspace, runs every service and Vite (hot reload); Rust changes rebuild and restart the services. `-- --only notes,edge`, `-- --no-web` |
| `npm run build` | Type-check, build the web app into `web/dist` and release binaries of every service |
| `npm start` | Run the release builds; the edge serves the web app and the API on `EDGE_PORT` |
| `npm test` | Vitest (web) and `cargo test --workspace` |
| `npm run check` | ESLint + clippy, Prettier + rustfmt, vue-tsc and all tests — the quality gate |
| `npm run lint` / `npm run format` | Linters only / format everything |
| `npm run setup` | Create `.env` with a fresh `MASTER_KEY`; `-- --port-base 9000` moves every port |

## Configuration

All settings live in `.env` in the project root, read by every service, the web build and the scripts. It is git-ignored; `.env.example` documents every key and is committed.

| Key | Value | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_NAME` | `{{ env.APP_NAME }}` | App name shown in the UI and returned by the API |
| `APP_SLUG` | `{{ env.APP_SLUG }}` | Machine-friendly name ({% if features.auth %}session cookie, {% endif %}logs) |
| `DB_PATH` | `{{ env.DB_PATH }}` | SQLite file shared by the services, relative to the project root |
| `MASTER_KEY` | generated | Encrypts secrets at rest; keep it secret and never change it on a running installation |
| `EDGE_PORT` | `{{ ports.EDGE_PORT }}` | Public entry: API proxy and the built web app |
{%- if features.auth %}
| `IDENTITY_PORT` | `{{ ports.IDENTITY_PORT }}` | Identity service (accounts, sessions, API keys) |
{%- endif %}
| `NOTES_PORT` | `{{ ports.NOTES_PORT }}` | Notes service (the example) |
| `WEB_PORT` | `{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}` | Vite dev server |
| `BIND_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Interface the services listen on |
| `PUBLIC_URL` | empty | URL users open{% if features.auth %}; `https://` makes cookies secure{% endif %} |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `error`, `warn`, `info`, `debug`, `trace` or a `RUST_LOG` filter |
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}
| `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` | `{{ project.slug }}` | Docker Compose project name |
| `DOCKER_DATA` | `{{ env.DOCKER_DATA }}` | Where the container keeps the database: `data` (Docker volume) or `./data` (project folder) |
{%- endif %}

## Project structure

```text
crates/core/     shared library: config, service registry, database, errors, crypto, bootstrap
services/edge/   reverse proxy by services.json + the built web app
{%- if features.auth %}
services/identity/  accounts, sessions, personal API keys
{%- endif %}
services/notes/  example service (CRUD over its own table)
migrations/      SQL migrations, applied by every service at start
web/             Vue 3 + Vite app: app shell, shared UI kit, feature modules in src/features/
scripts/         setup, dev runner, production runner
docs/            architecture, HTTP API, frontend modules
```

Read `docs/architecture.md` to add a service, a migration or a web module.
{%- if features.auth %}

## Accounts

The first registered user becomes the administrator. Users sign in with an email and password (a session cookie) or call the API with a personal key: `Authorization: Bearer <key>` (create keys on the API keys page). Administrators can list all users with `GET /api/admin/users` (see `docs/api.md`).
{%- endif %}
